---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Tyranids Beginner's Guide — Warhammer 40k"
  description="New to Tyranids? Learn the Hive Mind lore, how the swarm plays on the table, how to paint a whole horde fast, and what to buy first."
>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="px-6 pt-16 pb-12 border-b border-[#2a2a35]">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/factions" class="text-sm text-[#4a4855] hover:text-[#8a8590] transition-colors mb-6 inline-block">
        ← All Factions
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-6">
        <div class="text-6xl">🐛</div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-[#c9a84c] text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase mb-2 font-display">Faction Guide</p>
          <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">Tyranids</h1>
          <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
            A living swarm from beyond the galaxy, driven by a single psychic will: consume everything. 
            No mercy, no malice, no individual thought. Just hunger on an extinction-level scale.
            One of the most unique and visually striking armies in the game.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Quick stats -->
      <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Playstyle</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">Fast Swarm</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Painting</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-green-400">Easy ✓</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Rules</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-yellow-400">Medium</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Starter Cost</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">~$160–$220</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Lore -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">Who are the Tyranids?</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg">
        <p>
          They don't come from the Milky Way. They come from the void between galaxies — 
          the lightless space where nothing lives. Nobody knows what drove them here. 
          Nobody knows how many more are coming. What's known is that the first Hive Fleets 
          to arrive were not the main fleet. They were the scouts.
        </p>
        <p>
          A Tyranid Hive Fleet is a living organism on a galactic scale. Every creature 
          in the swarm — from the smallest ripper to the towering Hive Tyrant — 
          is a cell in a single body, controlled by the Hive Mind. 
          There are no generals, no orders, no dissent. 
          Every being acts with perfect coordination toward a single purpose.
        </p>
        <p>
          That purpose is consumption. When a Hive Fleet reaches a planet, 
          it doesn't destroy it — it <em>eats</em> it. Every tree, every animal, 
          every human, every microbe is broken down into raw biomatter. 
          That biomatter is processed back into the fleet to birth new creatures, 
          new weapons, new adaptations. Nothing is wasted. 
          When they're done, the planet is a lifeless rock.
        </p>
        <p>
          The most terrifying thing about the Tyranids isn't their numbers. 
          It's that they <em>adapt</em>. If a weapon kills them effectively, 
          the next wave is immune to it. They study every enemy, 
          evolve a counter, and keep coming. There is no "winning" against the Tyranids. 
          There is only surviving long enough to matter.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Hive Fleets -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">Pick your Hive Fleet</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-8 text-lg">
        Like Space Marine Chapters, Hive Fleets give you distinct colors and special rules. 
        This is your biggest aesthetic decision — Tyranids can look wildly different depending on your scheme.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        {[
          {
            name: 'Hive Fleet Leviathan',
            colors: 'White & Purple',
            swatch1: 'bg-purple-700',
            swatch2: 'bg-gray-100',
            painting: 'Medium',
            paintColor: 'text-yellow-400',
            desc: 'The largest and most dangerous Hive Fleet currently threatening the galaxy. Classic, striking color scheme — pale bone body with deep purple chitin plates. The "official" look from GW\'s marketing.',
          },
          {
            name: 'Hive Fleet Behemoth',
            colors: 'Red & Blue',
            swatch1: 'bg-red-700',
            swatch2: 'bg-blue-700',
            painting: 'Easy',
            paintColor: 'text-green-400',
            desc: 'The first Hive Fleet to breach Imperial space at scale — it devastated Ultramar and wiped out the Ultramarines\' entire 1st Company at the Battle for Macragge. Bold red and blue is easy to paint and looks aggressive on the table.',
          },
          {
            name: 'Hive Fleet Kraken',
            colors: 'Red & Bone',
            swatch1: 'bg-red-600',
            swatch2: 'bg-amber-200',
            painting: 'Easy',
            paintColor: 'text-green-400',
            desc: 'Known for speed and overwhelming multiple-front attacks. Warm red chitin with bone-colored flesh — one of the easiest schemes to execute and looks fantastic with contrast paints.',
          },
          {
            name: 'Custom Hive Fleet',
            colors: 'Your choice',
            swatch1: 'bg-gradient-to-r from-green-700 to-teal-600',
            swatch2: 'bg-emerald-400',
            painting: 'Varies',
            paintColor: 'text-[#8a8590]',
            desc: 'Many players invent their own Hive Fleet with completely custom colors — green and black, orange and bone, teal and white. Tyranids reward creative schemes more than almost any other faction.',
          },
        ].map(fleet => (
          <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
              <div class="flex gap-1 flex-shrink-0">
                <div class={`w-3 h-12 rounded-l ${fleet.swatch1}`}></div>
                <div class={`w-3 h-12 rounded-r ${fleet.swatch2}`}></div>
              </div>
              <div class="flex-1">
                <div class="flex items-center flex-wrap gap-3 mb-1">
                  <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-lg">{fleet.name}</h3>
                  <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">{fleet.colors}</span>
                  <span class={`text-xs font-semibold ${fleet.paintColor}`}>Painting: {fleet.painting}</span>
                </div>
                <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm leading-relaxed">{fleet.desc}</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Playstyle -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">How they play on the table</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg mb-10">
        <p>
          Tyranids are a <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">fast, aggressive swarm</strong>. 
          They flood the table with cheap fast troops — Hormagaunts, Termagants, Rippers — 
          while bigger creatures like Warriors and Carnifexes support and lead the charge.
        </p>
        <p>
          The army's key mechanic is <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Synapse</strong>. 
          Larger Tyranid creatures (called Synapse creatures) project a psychic field that 
          keeps nearby smaller units focused and effective. Push your Synapse creatures 
          forward and your swarm operates like a machine. Lose them and smaller units 
          start acting on instinct — still dangerous, but less controlled.
        </p>
        <p>
          You have two main army styles to choose from. 
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Swarm</strong> lists flood the board with 50–80 
          small models and overwhelm opponents with sheer numbers. 
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Nidzilla</strong> lists go the opposite direction — 
          fewer, bigger creatures. A Hive Tyrant, several Carnifexes, a Screamer-Killer. 
          Slower but terrifying to face and far fewer models to paint.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-green-400">Tyranids are for you if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✓ You love the alien, biomechanical aesthetic</li>
            <li>✓ You want a fast, aggressive playstyle</li>
            <li>✓ You want total creative freedom on colors</li>
            <li>✓ You want big impressive monster models</li>
            <li>✓ You want an army that feels genuinely alien — no guns, no mercy</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-red-400">Maybe look elsewhere if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✗ You want a strong shooting army</li>
            <li>✗ You don't want to assemble and paint 50+ small models</li>
            <li>✗ You want a disciplined, structured playstyle</li>
            <li>✗ You prefer human or humanoid armies</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Painting -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">How to paint Tyranids</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-4 text-lg">Using Hive Fleet Kraken (red chitin + bone flesh) — the easiest scheme for beginners.</p>
      <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] mb-10 leading-relaxed">
        Tyranids are one of the best armies for contrast paints. The organic shapes — 
        muscle, chitin plates, tendons — are exactly what contrast paints were designed for. 
        You can paint a Hormagaunt to a great tabletop standard in under 15 minutes.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4 mb-10">
        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">1</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Spray Wraithbone</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">The warm cream base coat is essential for Contrast paints to look their best. Don't substitute grey — it'll change all your colors.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">2</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Blood Angels Red Contrast on all chitin plates</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">The hard, raised armor sections. One coat self-shades — darker in the recesses, brighter on the raised areas. Looks great immediately.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">3</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Skeleton Horde Contrast on flesh and muscle</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">The soft, organic body areas — legs, torso, head. Bone-colored with instant shadow in all the muscle crevices. One coat.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">4</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Casandora Yellow shade wash on talons and claws</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Optional but striking — gives the claws a distinct amber color that reads well from a distance and breaks up the red/bone.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">5</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Drybrush Wraithbone over the flesh areas</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Light drybrush on raised muscles brings the highlights back and gives the flesh a dry, sinew-like quality. Takes 30 seconds per model.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">6</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Pick out eyes with Moot Green, base the model</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">A single dot of bright green in each eye socket makes the model pop from across the table. Base with a brown or grey texture paint and a tuft.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-5">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-2">Batch painting is everything</h3>
        <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm leading-relaxed">
          With Tyranids, you'll often paint 10–20 identical small models at once. 
          Line them all up on a strip of cardboard. Do step 1 on all of them. 
          Move to step 2 on all of them. Each pass takes minutes and you finish a squad 
          in the same time it takes to do one model carefully. 
          This is how Tyranid players paint 60-model armies without losing their mind.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- What to buy -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">What to buy first</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-10 text-lg">One box. Paint it. Then decide if you're going swarm or monsters — they need very different second purchases.</p>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-4">
          <span class="bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] text-xs font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-display mr-2">Start Here</span>
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$160</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Combat Patrol: Tyranids</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          Includes a Parasite of Mortrex (fast, terrifying winged leader), 10 Genestealers 
          (lightning-fast melee shock troops), 3 Tyrant Guard or Hive Guard (heavy support), 
          a Biovore or Pyrovore (ranged or melee artillery), and 3 Spore Mines. 
          A compact assault force that hits fast and hits hard.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FJ8RTK8P?tag=grimdarkprime-20"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Buy on Amazon →
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Second purchase options -->
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-6">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] mb-3">If you want to go swarm → ~$55</p>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-2">Termagants (24-model box)</h3>
          <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Your core troop. Flood the board with them. Fast to paint in batches and exactly what opponents don't want to deal with.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] mb-3">If you want to go monsters → ~$70</p>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-2">Carnifex</h3>
          <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">A tank on legs. One of the most iconic 40k models. Customize with different bio-weapon arms. Incredibly satisfying to paint and play.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Paints -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-4">Paints you need (Kraken scheme)</h3>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          {[
            { name: 'Wraithbone Spray', use: 'Base coat — essential for contrast paints', required: true },
            { name: 'Blood Angels Red (Contrast)', use: 'Chitin plates — one coat, self-shading', required: true },
            { name: 'Skeleton Horde (Contrast)', use: 'Flesh and muscle areas', required: true },
            { name: 'Casandora Yellow (Shade)', use: 'Wash on talons and claws for amber tint', required: true },
            { name: 'Moot Green', use: 'Eye dots — one tiny dot per eye', required: false },
            { name: 'Wraithbone (pot)', use: 'Drybrush on flesh highlights', required: false },
          ].map(paint => (
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class={`text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 font-display ${paint.required ? 'bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113]' : 'border border-[#2a2a35] text-[#4a4855]'}`}>
                {paint.required ? 'Essential' : 'Optional'}
              </span>
              <div>
                <span class="text-sm font-semibold">{paint.name}</span>
                <span class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm"> — {paint.use}</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-4 italic">~$32 for the essentials. Contrast paints are slightly more expensive but do the work of three paints in one.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Cost breakdown -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-8">Honest cost breakdown</h2>
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
        {[
          { item: 'Combat Patrol: Tyranids', cost: '~$160', note: 'Parasite of Mortrex, Genestealers, Tyrant Guard, Biovore' },
          { item: 'Essential paints (4 Contrast + spray)', cost: '~$32', note: 'Wraithbone spray + 3 contrast paints' },
          { item: 'Basing supplies', cost: '~$12', note: 'Texture paint + tufts' },
          { item: 'Clippers + hobby knife', cost: '~$20', note: 'One-time purchase' },
          { item: 'Superglue', cost: '~$5', note: 'Multi-part models need glue' },
        ].map((row, i) => (
          <div class={`flex items-start justify-between px-5 py-4 gap-4 ${i % 2 === 0 ? '' : 'bg-[#111113]'}`}>
            <div>
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold">{row.item}</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] mt-0.5">{row.note}</p>
            </div>
            <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] flex-shrink-0">{row.cost}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-4 bg-[#1f1d14] border-t border-[#c9a84c]">
          <p class="font-display font-semibold">All-in starter total</p>
          <span class="font-display font-bold text-[#c9a84c] text-lg">~$229</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-4 italic">
        Swarm players: budget for Termagants next (~$55 for 24). Monster players: budget for a Carnifex (~$70). 
        Both are very different second purchases — paint the patrol first to know which direction you want.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="px-6 py-20 text-center">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold mb-4">The Hive hungers.</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg mb-8">
        Pick your Hive Fleet colors, grab the Combat Patrol, and start painting in batches of ten. 
        The swarm builds itself one model at a time.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
        <a
          href="/painting"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded text-lg transition-colors font-display tracking-wide"
        >
          Painting Guide →
        </a>
        <a
          href="/quiz"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded text-lg transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Retake the Quiz
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
